<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <AssemblyName>einzel-mcp</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>Einzel.Mcp</RootNamespace>
    <Description>
      The live-session server. Spec figure 3 puts the CLI, this server and the
      shell side by side as peers rather than as a stack, and figure 6 says what
      distinguishes this one: loop A is a project folder and needs no protocol,
      while loop B is a human with the shell open and an agent joining them on
      the same model. So the server's subject is the shared session - one
      document, two parties, one attributed and linear journal (MCP-1) - and not
      a second spelling of the CLI.

      An executable so that stdio works with no shell, and a library so that the
      shell can host the same tools in process over streamable HTTP, which is
      the primary transport the specification names.
    </Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Einzel.Commands\Einzel.Commands.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="ModelContextProtocol.Core" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
